D. PARITY / IMPLEMENTATION NOTES (web RegenEfficiencyWidget.tsx → native)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
• Data sources bound via the P1/S8 state-holder seam (RegenEfficiencySource → RegenUpdate
  → RegenEfficiencyModel); NO HTTP in the view. Mirrors useRegenEfficiency / useVehicles /
  useUnits. RegenEfficiencyInput mirrors the wire RegenEfficiencyData
  (totalRegenWh, totalDriveWh, regenRatio, monthlyAvgRegen, freeCharges).
• SI at rest, convert at the display boundary: formatEnergy Wh→kWh and formatPower W→kW
  (web DEFAULT_ENERGY_PREF='kWh' / DEFAULT_POWER_PREF='kW', precision 1, '—' fallback),
  fmtInt for free charges, ${Math.round(regenPct)}% for the gauge.
• regenColor parity: >30% success, >15% warning, else danger — mapped to SI status tokens.
• Composition: web WidgetGaugeHero → native RegenGaugeRing (Swift radial gauge, Reduce-Motion
  aware) + three RegenStatTiles; web isCompact = size.cols <= 1 reproduced (registry default
  1×2 renders the compact gauge-only tile; ≥2 cols add the titled header + stats + help popover).
• States reproduced: loading (skeleton) / empty (EmptyState "No regen data") / error
  (QueryError + Retry) / content, plus live / stale / offline freshness + auto-refresh.
• i18n: every web key resolves through the P1/S10 facade (RegenEfficiencyStrings, table
  "RegenEfficiencyWidget") — title, totalKwh, monthlyAvg, freeCharges, recovery, noData,
  help.regenEfficiency.body, description — no English literals in code.
• a11y: VoiceOver labels on every control + a testable RegenEfficiencyAccessibility.summary;
  Dynamic Type via minimumScaleFactor; Reduce-Motion honored on the gauge arc.
• Telemetry: view.opened emitted once with surface slug "RegenEfficiencyWidget" (P1/S11).
• Charts/maps: none in this surface (web source uses none).

